    "meta": {
      "references": [
        {
          "title": "Pro Display ClearView holographic rear projection film",
          "url": "https://prodisplay.com/projection-screens/rear-projection/clearview-holographic-display/",
          "accessed": "2026-08-12",
          "usedFor": "glass wall: >=85% transmission, gain 1.2-1.8, 120H/60V viewing"
        },
        {
          "title": "Ultraleap - How big is the Leap Motion Controller 2",
          "url": "https://support.ultraleap.com/hc/en-us/articles/12853399254813-How-big-is-the-Leap-Motion-Controller-2",
          "accessed": "2026-08-12",
          "usedFor": "84 x 20 x 12 mm, 160x160 FOV, 10-110 cm range - the pinch detector"
        },
        {
          "title": "Orbbec Femto Bolt hardware specifications",
          "url": "https://www.orbbec.com/documentation/femto-bolt-hardware-specifications/",
          "accessed": "2026-08-12",
          "usedFor": "115 x 40 x 65 mm, WFOV 120x120, 0.25-5.46 m - both depth volumes"
        },
        {
          "title": "Microsoft Research - LightSpace",
          "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/project/lightspace/",
          "accessed": "2026-08-12",
          "usedFor": "multiple overlapping depth volumes so a hand stays tracked BETWEEN surfaces - the precedent for the mat-to-wall drag"
        },
        {
          "title": "Sony Xperia Touch - IR array + 60 fps camera touch detection",
          "url": "https://www.photoxels.com/sony-xperia-touch-is-an-interactive-projector-that-combines-infrared-light-array-with-60fps-camera-capture-to-turn-any-flat-surface-into-a-23-inch-hd-touchscreen-for-apps-games-online-video-chat/",
          "accessed": "2026-08-12",
          "usedFor": "850 nm IR plane grazing the mat for true touch vs hover"
        }
      ],
      "anchorProportions": [
        "desk top height = 740 mm (seated standard)",
        "mat = 1220 x 762 mm = 4ft 0in x 2ft 6in, aspect 1.601:1 == native 16:10 (WUXGA), so the projector maps 1:1 with no letterboxing",
        "rear UST throw ratio 0.25 -> lens sits exactly 450 mm behind the 1800 mm wide glass wall",
        "overhead projector drop = 1135 mm over a 1220 mm image -> 0.93:1 short throw",
        "glass wall bottom at y=850, i.e. 110 mm clear above the desktop, so it reads as a wall surface rather than a monitor",
        "transfer corridor = mat back edge z=-541 to glass wall z=-690, i.e. a 149 mm reach plus a 110 mm lift. The two ToF volumes must both cover it or a dragged object drops out of tracking mid-flight"
      ],
      "calloutLayout": "One column per side: elbows at x=-1500 and x=+1500, all on a common z=-300 plane, fanned on a 320 mm vertical ladder from y=2900 down. Rows are ordered by anchor height so no leader line crosses another inside a column, and the shared elbow plane is what stops them piling up under the iso perspective. Anchors are LOCAL to each part, so moving a part takes its callout with it.",
      "interactionModel": "Two display surfaces treated as one desktop, like dual monitors. Surface A = the projected mat (touch via the IR plane). Surface B = the glass wall (rear-projected). A pinch is detected by the Leap in the near field, the hand is then handed off between the two ToF volumes as it lifts off the mat and moves back toward the wall, and the object follows. Software is out of scope here; this models the hardware that makes it possible."
    },
